# Tests and validation

- Keep tests deterministic and isolated; avoid network/time randomness unless explicitly under test.
- Prefer focused test updates that match behavior changes; do not rewrite broad fixtures unless required.
- When fixing regressions, add or adjust at least one assertion that would fail before the fix.
- Validate touched test suites with targeted commands first, then expand only if failures suggest cross-area impact.
- In final handoff, include exact test commands run and outcomes (pass/fail/skip).

## Rule self-review

When this rule materially guided the task, follow **Rules self-review** in `autopulse-execution.mdc` and apply it to this file.
